          "entradaId": "freeman-636",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Mark 1:39; Luke 4:44. Jewish writers claim for the synagogue a very remote antiquity, but its origin probably dates during the captivity. There were no fixed proportions in the building, as there were in the tabernacle and in the temple. When a synagogue was to be built…"
      },
      "c-fa5234d94474e9ed": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-635",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Luke 4:9. This is commonly supposed to have been the summit of the royal gallery built by Herod within the area of the temple building’s on the edge of the Kedron valley. Josephus says of it: “This cloister deserves to be mentioned better than any other under the sun; fo…"
      }
